==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AuditUniqueToAttempt  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditUniqueToAttempt.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets Alloy invent a state in which two AccessAttempts share a single AuditEntry — i.e., an audit entry has been re-bound/mutated. The injection forces such an instance to exist, so the append-only and 1:1-audit assertions must fail.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, AuditCompleteness, FR_015_AuditImmutable, FR_013_AuditEveryAccess
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_AuditImmutable: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_AuditEveryAccess: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermittedRequiresAllowed  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_PermittedRequiresAllowed.als
    rationale: Clearing this load-bearing fact removes the constraint that a Permitted outcome lies in a documented Allowed cell. The injection forces a clinician-on-GetAccessLog Permitted attempt (a denied cell in the matrix); LeastPrivilege and the role-specific FRs must find it.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_007_ComplianceNoClinicalContent, FR_018_ComplianceOnlyAccessLog, FR_005_ClinicianNoAccessLog
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_007_ComplianceNoClinicalContent: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_ComplianceOnlyAccessLog: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_005_ClinicianNoAccessLog: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeniedEnvelope  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_DeniedEnvelope.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the envelope vary across denied responses. The injection forces two denied attempts to have different envelopes — the existence-leak the byte-equivalent 403 envelope is designed to prevent.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_ByteEquivalentForbidden: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ClinicianCareTeamGate  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_ClinicianCareTeamGate.als
    rationale: Removes the structural care-team requirement on permitted clinician access. The injection forces a clinician to be permitted on GetRecord with no matching CareTeamMembership, which is exactly the FR-004 / SC-010 violation pattern.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_004_CareTeamGating
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_004_CareTeamGating: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AuditAttribution  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_AuditAttribution.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact lets the audit entry's recorded accessor/role/op/outcome drift from the attempt that produced it. The injection forces a recorded-accessor mismatch, which is exactly the misattribution pattern the assertions guard against.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_014_AuditFields
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_014_AuditFields: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoteUniqueToAttempt  → runs/C-L3/mutated_F_NoteUniqueToAttempt.als
    rationale: Clearing this fact allows the same ClinicalNote to be bound to two distinct AccessAttempts — i.e., a note has been re-pointed or duplicated, the structural shadow of mutation/deletion. The injection forces two attempts to share one note.
    expected to FAIL: NoSelfMutation, FR_012_AppendOnlyNotes, AppendOnly
      - NoSelfMutation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_012_AppendOnlyNotes: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

